  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Measles outbreak response in 10 most affected districts in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to strengthen the Measles outbreak response in the 10 most affected districts in Zimbabwe. This project supports the immunization processes as well as operational expenses related to the measles epidemic response. The assistance helps increase measles vaccination coverage, build the required herd immunity and stop the spread of the disease. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 1,370,756 people, including  657,963 boys and 712,793  girls, and 137,075  persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
